# qmllint counts per shell and category, as of the last update.
# tools/qml-lint.sh fails when a count grows past its number here.
# Lower a number whenever you fix something. Never raise one to make the check pass, with one exception:
# an increase the owner has decided to accept, recorded below as a '#!' line with its reason
# (tools/tests/test_qml_baseline.py checks the record). Rewriting the baseline keeps those lines.
#! accepted 2026-10-24 bar uncreatable-type 7->10 Configs/.config/quickshell/bar/modules/minibar/view/MiniBar.qml:16: one per window of this shell, which qmllint reports as "not creatable" because Quickshell supplies the backend at runtime; 7->8 was the bar editor (CI run 38745431293) and 8->9 is the minimal bar's window, 9->10 the notes window (bar/modules/notes/NotesWindow.qml:11, accepted by the owner on 2026-11-24); inherent to having the window, and it goes only by not having one (measured locally, tools/qml-lint.sh --since, 2026-10-24)
bar 13 import
bar 4 incompatible-type
bar 148 missing-property
bar 2 property-override
bar 10 uncreatable-type
bar 84 unqualified
bar 5 unresolved-type
